into the number of chips you have?

261
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:40,650
Wait a sec!

262
00:13:40,733 --> 00:13:42,197
My lifetime income is pathetic!

263
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:44,517
I can't believe I have
less than Ronko or Nogomi!

264
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,417
And you have way too much over there!

265
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:47,382
Of course I do.

266
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,444
This mistress is making a move.

267
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,717
She's going all in.

268
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:54,380
It's a super duper chance! Yay!

269
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:56,720
Please, show your hand.

270
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,220
Ooh, the suspense! And open!

271
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:04,300
Three of a kind. Two
of a kind. Three, nine!

272
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:09,077
I thought I had a pretty
good shot with that

273
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:12,000
hand three nine can't
beat a five-five I guess?

274
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:13,760
Stupid piglet!

275
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:19,217
Whatever, that's one down if you have no
chips left to make your way over there?

276
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:20,130
Please.

277
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:21,130
What?

278
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:27,870
Damn.

279
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:29,080
Ah, shit.

280
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:37,200
Excuse me, is this the winning hand?

281
00:14:40,260 --> 00:14:41,090
Mother.

282
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,140
What happens if we lose all the chips?

283
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:45,832
According to the rumors?

284
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:50,820
Up in the bitter cold of the Bering
Sea, You catch craps without rest.

285
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:55,987
Apparently, they wear you down until no
one would ever recognize you as a maid.

286
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,780
For real? Too funny.

287
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:00,317
So what are we going to do?

288
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,576
It's time for the next game to begin.

289
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:05,460
Then allow me to go first. Hey, Ronko.

290
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:09,737
What would you do if I asked you to
entrust me with all of your poker chips?

291
00:15:09,820 --> 00:15:10,680
Then I would.

292
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:14,320
Both my chips and my life.
Thank you. That means a lot.

293
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:25,127
Looks like Yamichi's
gonna use Ronko's chips.

294
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:28,037
Then if she loses, that
means we're done for?

295
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,457
You've got this, piglet!

296
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:30,370
Come on!

297
00:15:30,453 --> 00:15:31,689
The chief believes in you!

298
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:34,000
She's the last one, huh?

299
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:38,760
Alright, where should we ship off
those not-so-stellar pork butts?

300
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:48,920
First betting round is in play.

301
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:52,600
A raise.

302
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:57,057
With this move, this mistress here has
doubled the wager, increasing the pot.

303
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:59,880
It's a super duper big chance! Yay!

304
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:03,017
That customer's awfully
confident with her hand.

305
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,397
Makes me want to step up.

306
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,598
That should make things interesting.

307
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,600
What a dumb maid.

308
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:10,801
You have zero chances of winning.

309
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:12,480
She calls.

310
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:21,300
Check, please. Me too.

311
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:26,820
All right, it's the final betting round.

312
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:29,900
I'd like to raise.

313
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:32,439
That increases the wager eightfold.

314
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:36,440
It's the super duper last
and final chance. Yay!

315
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:41,217
Yumiichi, you've got this, I hope.

316
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:43,300
You know what you're doing, right?

317
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:45,600
No, no, no, no, no.

318
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:47,277
She could lose everything.

319
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:50,117
I hear the Bering Sea gets
down to minus 30 degrees.

320
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,777
They say if you fall in the
water, you die in three seconds.

321
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:53,690
No way.

322
00:16:53,773 --> 00:16:54,697
There's no freaking way.

323
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:55,610
Well, dang it.

324
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:57,597
Yumiichi had today's best horoscope.

325
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:59,197
I thought for sure she'd win.

326
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:00,515
What are we gonna do?

327
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:01,915
What are we gonna do?

328
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:03,811
It's your turn, mistress.

329
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:07,540
If you don't fold, it'll
be game over right now.

330
00:17:23,860 --> 00:17:24,800
I'm all in.

331
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,497
I can't believe she went for it.

332
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,700
Is that wise to do?

333
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:30,680
Maybe she's all like, whatevs. Why?

334
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:32,720
There's no way she can win.

335
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,734
Why is she going for it with that hand?

336
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:41,680
Alright, please show your
hands in a clockwise direction.

337
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:46,220
Now, Mistress, please show us your hand.

338
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:51,012
You can't call yourself a maid
with that level of service.

339
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:54,877
Did you think I wouldn't
notice what you were doing?

340
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:55,837
During the game,

341
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:57,817
you never deal out the
top card to your associate

342
00:17:57,900 --> 00:18:00,297
over there in order to
cheat your way to a win.

343
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:01,210
What?

344
00:18:01,293 --> 00:18:02,123
The dealer's cheating?

345
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:03,060
That's not fair.

346
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,617
Not fair at all, hustler.

347
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:07,037
Better go back to your
hometown and start over, bitch.

348
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:10,117
You won some and lost some,
so we wouldn't ever catch on.

349
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:11,517
But when you're dealt a winning hand,

350
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:15,424
you have a bad habit of always
fiddling around with your glasses.

351
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:18,742
I see right through your tricks.

352
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:22,077
That confident bet was a bluff
to dupe me out of my winnings.

353
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,057
You didn't touch your glasses this time.

354
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,846
That means I have the
winning hand this round.

355
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:29,377
Mistress, what are you talking about?

356
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:30,700
Yumechi! Good one.

357
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:31,837
I knew you could do it.

358
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:32,760
Yeah, go!

359
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:46,120
A full house and a full house.

360
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,180
Did Yumechi just win the game?

361
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:50,600
No, she didn't. She lost. What?

362
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:08,410
Well, okay.

363
00:19:08,740 --> 00:19:10,446
That was a good game, ladies.

364
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:14,177
Oh, wow, what a great game.

365
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:16,400
So very moving. Asshole.

366
00:19:16,540 --> 00:19:18,775
Well, then, please come over this way.

367
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,058
Go ahead, go ahead.

368
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:23,077
All right, piggies, you'll
be departing at 2100.

369
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,337
I ain't going on no boat
to go crab catching.

370
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:27,157
My cafe, give me back my cafe.

371
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:29,040
You damn whining, pig turd.

372
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:31,237
You're going to delay our
shipment port for brains.

373
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:33,097
Time is money in this business.

374
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:35,737
You should have enough
sense to know that, right?

375
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:39,857
Think you crappy maids know better than
garbage can run a cafe here at Akiva,

376
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:40,770
of all places?

377
00:19:40,853 --> 00:19:42,640
Maybe in like 50,000 years?

378
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,177
What the...

379
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:56,700
That's too funny.

380
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:02,437
We'll be taking back our cafe.

381
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:05,197
You lost wine, so get back in the cage!

382
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:06,757
Shut up, bitch.

383
00:20:06,840 --> 00:20:08,557
You're the one who swindled us.

384
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:11,037
We're the ones struggling
and putting it hard.

385
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:12,500
Honest work.

386
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:22,517
This sucks!

387
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:23,897
Let's finish this shit.

388
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:25,857
Gosh, I haven't used a gun in ages.

389
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:26,940
There it is.

390
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,920
Hey, get back here, pigs!

391
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:45,540
I'll make you maids in hell with this!

392
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:50,040
Allow me to send you to hell.

393
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:27,100
There was an explosion last
night at a building in Akihabara.

394
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:31,377
According to investigators, it was due
to a skirmish in an underground casino.

395
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:34,897
This establishment had close
connections to a loan shark business.

396
00:21:34,980 --> 00:21:35,810
So sad.

397
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:37,469
That's really awful stuff.

398
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:40,217
Apparently, it's not all
that unusual these days.

399
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:42,535
That explosion was a little too risky.

400
00:21:42,940 --> 00:21:46,822
Ours from fireworks looks like
we're celebrating New Year's early.

401
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:49,940
But you know, the loan
sharks got in the cafe safe.

402
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:51,977
I think I did good, didn't I?

403
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:53,937
Uh, we're still behind on our dues.

404
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:57,377
I'm sure someone is going to come
by soon asking for it the soy sauce.

405
00:21:57,460 --> 00:21:58,754
May I take it, please?

406
00:21:59,340 --> 00:22:00,170
Sure.

407
00:22:03,460 --> 00:22:07,240
I need to calm down at
least I'm still alive.

408
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:28,660
Today and tomorrow are all good.

409
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:32,047
We're all good at the house.

410
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:37,057
We're all good at the house.

411
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:40,440
That's the truth of our life.

412
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:45,457
You're not stupid to be kidding me.

413
00:22:45,540 --> 00:22:48,240
We're all good at the blood.

414
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:57,000
Thank you.

415
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:23,177
Thank you so

416
00:23:23,260 --> 00:23:28,957
much

417
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:31,417
for

418
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:32,880
watching.
